From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:11:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: keyboard hint line and type-ahead on the lock screen
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

LOCKSCREEN_SECURE_ENTRY_UX for phones with a hardware keyboard and no
number row (Q25: Alt, Shift, Sym, letters):

* Hint line: with a QWERTY keyboard the lock screen indication area
  adds "Type PIN · Enter unlocks" ("Type password · Enter unlocks",
  or "Enter unlocks" for a swipe lock; none for a pattern). The
  credential type is read off the main thread. Nothing shows without a
  hardware keyboard.
* Type-ahead: a printable key from a physical keyboard on the locked
  glance of a secure keyguard opens the primary bouncer, as Enter
  already does, and is typed into the PIN or password field when that
  field resumes, together with any key typed while it was opening.
  The keys are held in SableKeyguardTypeAhead for at most 3 s after
  the last one, are cleared when taken, never logged, and nothing is
  checked or submitted: Enter still submits. Confirm, Back, Escape,
  Tab and delete keys, repeats and Ctrl/Meta/Fn chords keep their
  meaning; focused notification rows keep their commands.
* PIN keys wherever focus is: KeyguardSecurityContainerController
  offers every key (the shade window root calls interceptMediaKey
  before the view tree) to the PIN view while it is shown, and the PIN
  view also handles them in dispatchKeyEvent. Upstream, keys reached it
  only through the password field's key listener, so with focus on an
  on-screen digit, or nowhere in the window, typed digits were lost
  and Enter pressed the focused digit. Digits are the number row, the
  numpad, the key map's Alt digit or phone-pad number and, for a plain
  or Alt press, the phone-pad letters W E R S D F Z X C = 1-9 by key
  code, so they also work when a keyboard layout overlay replaced the
  Q25 key map's number and alt entries; Shift and shortcut chords never
  give a digit. Digits act on a first DOWN through the on-screen keys
  (glance type-ahead first). Backspace deletes. Enter and numpad Enter
  act on the UP of a DOWN the view saw and always press OK. While a
  hardware keyboard is present (Configuration QWERTY) the on-screen
  keys are not focusable, so DPAD and Tab stay on the field; touch is
  unchanged.
* Bouncer hint: with a hardware keyboard the bouncer's default message
  gets the same hint as its second line ("Enter PIN" / "Type PIN ·
  Enter unlocks"); failure, lockout and biometric messages unchanged.

Legacy (non scene-container) keyguard only; the scene container path
is unchanged. Pure policy: keyguard/sable/SableKeyguardKeys.java and
SableKeyguardTypeAhead.java.
